# Direct runtime dependencies, human-edited.
#
# This is the file you change. The pinned, hash-checked lock that CI and the
# production host actually install from is generated with:
#
#   uv pip compile server/requirements.in --universal \
#     --python-version 3.10 --generate-hashes \
#     -o server/requirements.txt
#
# `--universal` is required, not cosmetic: it emits environment markers so one
# lock covers every interpreter from 3.10 up. A lock resolved for a single
# version pins conditional dependencies unconditionally - a 3.10 resolve pins
# backports-asyncio-runner, which refuses to install on 3.11 - so it would
# break the moment CI and the host disagreed on the Python version.

